The GUI sprites in mixins/justenoughitems/sprites.rs are JEI's own textures
(Common/src/main/resources/assets/jei/textures/gui/sprites, MIT), converted to
runs of pixels by tools/sprites.mjs.

The config screen (config.rs) follows MezzConfig GUI, the config screen JEI
26.3 opens, by mezz, https://github.com/mezz/MezzConfigGui (branch 26.3, MIT);
config_sprites.rs holds its textures
(Common/src/main/resources/assets/mezz_config/textures/mezz_config/atlas/gui)
and JEI's icon, converted by tools/configsprites.mjs.

This port rewrites JEI's ingredient list, bookmarks, search grammar and
recipes screen in Rust for Horizon's native mod API, from the game's own item
and recipe tables. Changes from the original: no plugin API (Horizon has no
Java mods to register categories); settings live on Horizon's mod settings
page; the creative tab (%) and identifier (&) search prefixes are on; colour
search (^) and the item-hiding edit mode are not ported. It is not affiliated
with mezz, Mojang or Microsoft.
